IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sk-sip`

-- The Saskatchewan Income Plan Act and The Seniors Income Plan Regulations -- the questions of the senior who receives, or
-- asks about, the Seniors Income Plan. Every question calls the rules in sk-sip.l4; nothing is restated here. Plain inputs,
-- one per fact the person can state. Amounts are monthly, in Canadian dollars.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quoted from the King's Printer consolidations, (c) 2026, Government of Saskatchewan; not an official
-- version. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Am I eligible`

@export Am I eligible for the Saskatchewan Seniors Income Plan under The Saskatchewan Income Plan Act s 4?
GIVEN `I make my home and am ordinarily in Saskatchewan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Saskatchewan is your home and you are ordinarily there
      `I am only a tourist, transient or visitor in Saskatchewan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in Saskatchewan only as a tourist, transient or visitor
      `I receive the Old Age Security pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive the monthly Old Age Security pension
      `I receive the Guaranteed Income Supplement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive the monthly Guaranteed Income Supplement (GIS)
      `my GIS is paid in another province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your GIS is being paid to you in another province
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for the Seniors Income Plan` IF
    `is eligible under Act s 4` (`is a resident under Act s 2(e)` `I make my home and am ordinarily in Saskatchewan` `I am only a tourist, transient or visitor in Saskatchewan`) `I receive the Old Age Security pension` `I receive the Guaranteed Income Supplement` `my GIS is paid in another province`

§ `How much will I get`

@export What is my maximum monthly Seniors Income Plan benefit under the Seniors Income Plan Regulations s 4?
GIVEN `my spouse's position` IS A `Spouse's OAS position` @desc Your spouse's or common-law partner's position: no spouse or partner; spouse or partner is a pensioner (receives OAS and GIS); spouse or partner is neither a pensioner nor receiving an allowance; or spouse or partner receives an allowance
      `I live in a special-care home or long-term hospital care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live in a designated special-care home, or are a long-term care patient in a hospital or health centre being charged a resident charge
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my maximum benefit` MEANS
    `the Reg s 4 maximum` (`the household for Reg s 4` `my spouse's position`) `I live in a special-care home or long-term hospital care`

@export How much Seniors Income Plan will I be paid each month under the Seniors Income Plan Regulations ss 4 to 6?
GIVEN `I am eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are eligible for the Seniors Income Plan (see the eligibility question)
      `my spouse's position` IS A `Spouse's OAS position` @desc Your spouse's or common-law partner's position: no spouse or partner; spouse or partner is a pensioner; spouse or partner is neither a pensioner nor receiving an allowance; or spouse or partner receives an allowance
      `I live in a special-care home or long-term hospital care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live in a designated special-care home, or are a long-term care patient being charged a resident charge
      `how much less than the maximum GIS I get` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum monthly GIS for your situation in the federal OAS Table of Rates, minus the GIS you actually receive, in dollars; 0 if you get the maximum
      `how much less than the maximum allowance my spouse gets` IS A NUMBER @desc If your spouse or partner receives the federal Allowance: the maximum Allowance minus what they receive, in dollars; 0 otherwise
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much will I be paid each month` MEANS
    `the monthly Seniors Income Plan benefit` `I am eligible` `my spouse's position` `I live in a special-care home or long-term hospital care` `how much less than the maximum GIS I get` `how much less than the maximum allowance my spouse gets`

§ `Changes and arrears`

@export If I move into or out of a special-care home, from which month does my Seniors Income Plan change, under the Regulations s 7?
GIVEN `the month I moved` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) in which you moved into or out of the facility
      `the year I moved` IS A NUMBER @desc The year in which you moved
GIVETH A `Month`
`From which month does my benefit change` MEANS `the Reg s 7 adjustment month` `the month I moved` `the year I moved`

@export If I was underpaid, from what date will the missing Seniors Income Plan be paid, under the Regulations s 9?
GIVEN `the date I became entitled` IS A DATE @desc The date from which you were entitled to the benefit (or to the higher amount)
      `the month the ministry found the error` IS A NUMBER @desc The month (1 to 12) in which the ministry discovered the underpayment
      `the year the ministry found the error` IS A NUMBER @desc The year in which the ministry discovered the underpayment
GIVETH A DATE
`From what date will arrears be paid` MEANS
    `the earliest date arrears are paid from` `the date I became entitled` `the month the ministry found the error` `the year the ministry found the error`

@export Does my Seniors Income Plan stop, under The Saskatchewan Income Plan Act s 7?
GIVEN `I am still eligible for the GIS` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are still eligible to receive the Guaranteed Income Supplement
      `my GIS is now paid in another province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your GIS is now being paid in another province
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my benefit stop` IF
    `payment ceases under Act s 7` `I am still eligible for the GIS` `my GIS is now paid in another province`

@export May an amount be deducted from my Seniors Income Plan, or the benefit be assigned or seized, under The Saskatchewan Income Plan Act ss 8 and 9?
GIVEN `it recovers an overpayment of the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the deduction is the ministry recovering an earlier overpayment of the Seniors Income Plan (rather than an assignment, charge, attachment or security given to someone else)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my benefit be reduced or taken` IF `a deduction from my benefit is allowed` `it recovers an overpayment of the benefit`
